      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C1"],
      "pins": ["C1.1", "C1.2"],
      "nets": ["Display_Power_Switch", "GND"],
      "observed": "On the EPD_Driver sheet the capacitor C1, connected between the Display_Power_Switch rail and GND (in parallel with C2), is drawn with the value '0.1uF/16V'.",
      "expected": "The specification lists C1 in the group of EPD capacitors that must match the Pervasive Displays default value of 1 uF / 25 V (the G1-specific 1 uF / 6.3 V value is placed on C2). C1 should therefore be 1 uF / 25 V, not 0.1 uF / 16 V.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "C1 0.1uF/16V (EPD_Driver.kicad_sch, page 3, right of the Display_Power_Switch label, next to C2 1uF/6.3V)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "| C2 default: 1 uF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 uF/25 V | Matches default |"}
      ],
      "impact": "The display-power/booster input node is decoupled with one tenth of the intended capacitance and a lower voltage rating than the PDI reference calls out; the EPD supply rail will have poorer decoupling/ripple performance than the intended design (and reduced margin if the node ever exceeds 16 V).",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design largely matches the specification, but the EPD driver sheet builds C1 as 0.1 uF / 16 V, whereas the specification explicitly places C1 in the group of PDI-matching display capacitors that must be 1 uF / 25 V, so the display-booster input decoupling deviates from the intended design."
}

